fact WorkItem(id: "WI-706", description: some(value: "Lambda-callback effect-row CONFORMANCE (WI-700 sibling / pre-existing hole, found by WI-700 /code-review). The WI-440/469 callback-row conformance check (validate_callback_effect_row) fires ONLY for an eta'd OP-REF callback arg -- it bails at arg_op_sym = extract_var_ref_sym_node(arg_occ)? for any non-var-ref arg, so a LAMBDA callback is unchecked against the declared callback row's lacks/closed constraints. Verified LOADING on HEAD af269943: shield[EffP={}](lambda () -> poke()) (poke rowed {Outside}, shield's callback declared () -> Int64 @ {EffP, -Outside}) loads with the lambda body's {Outside} escaping a -Outside slot into an effects {}-declared op; the eta twin ...(poke) correctly rejects. This is actual-vs-declared conformance for LAMBDAS -- DISTINCT from the self-contradiction shape of WI-705: here the declared row {-Outside} is consistent, but the lambda's INFERRED row {Outside} violates it. For External this is the memoize/CSE/Branch unsoundness proposal 054 section 'Branch and External' forbids, and a -External solver region is naturally an inline lambda. The false doc-comment claiming lambdas are 'checked elsewhere' was already corrected in WI-700 (typing.rs validate_callback_effect_row header). FIX: infer the lambda's effect row and run the same lacks/closed conformance, aligning the lambda's binder places to the declared callback param places. ACCEPTANCE: the lambda escape rejects; the eta/lambda twins agree; full cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-13T08:56:19Z"))

